        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Rochdale Pioneers\n- Organizations: Rochdale Society of Equitable Pioneers\n- Concepts: consumer co-operatives, patronage dividends, the modern co-operative movement\n\nFacts:\n- The Rochdale Society of Equitable Pioneers was founded in 1844 as an early consumer co-operative.\n- The Rochdale Society of Equitable Pioneers was one of the first organizations to pay a patronage dividend.\n- The Rochdale Society of Equitable Pioneers helped form the basis for the modern co-operative movement.\n- Working-class members of the Rochdale Society of Equitable Pioneers founded the first successful cooperative retail store in 1844.\n- The Rochdale Pioneers is a British biographical feature film released in 2012.\n- The Rochdale Pioneers tells the story of the foundation of the first successful cooperative retail store by working-class members of the Rochdale Society of Equitable Pioneers.",
